CRUD Operations – The Foundation of Web Development
  If you're learning web development, this is one of the first concepts you should master. Let’s break it down in the simplest way possible 👇
 
 🔄 CRUD stands for:
 ✅ C — CREATE (POST Method)
 This is when we want to add new data to the database.
  📍 Example: You fill a signup form and click “Register” — that’s a POST request to /users.
 
 👁️ R — READ (GET Method)
 This is how we retrieve data.
  📍 Example: Visiting your profile or user list — that’s a GET request to /users or /users/:id.
 
 🛠️ U — UPDATE (PUT Method)
 Want to edit your information? This is what happens behind the scenes.
  📍 Example: Changing your email or username — that's a PUT request to /users/:id.
 
 🗑️ D — DELETE (DELETE Method)
 As the name says, this removes data.
  📍 Example: Clicking “Delete Account” — sends a DELETE request to /users/:id.
 
 💡Why should you care?
  Every app you use—social media, e-commerce, booking systems—is built on these 4 operations.
 
 Understanding CRUD means you're one step closer to building your own real-world applications 🔥
